# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/sampler window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/sampler and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image, its stop rule and its minutes. The image is tp4-serve-6 throughout: SB builds it, the
# later jobs serve it, and a commit after SB's tag needs a new tag and every later job the new one.
# STt: the TIMING twin of the ST arm: c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace (c2-packed-tp4-speed: both verify audits OFF, the tail caps ON, no instruments, no stall watch)
# plus QWEN_FAST_PACKED_SAMPLER_IN_TRACE=1: the pinned sampler's ops are recorded inside the packed verify capture exactly as the T1 audit records them (and run in the warm forward), so every packed replay runs the sampler gathers on handles 0 then 1; output[3] is held but never read back and never compared per round, so no host sync is added.
# Run it after the five repeats on the diag twin pass (a hang here costs the card reset): read the round time and the coding
# decode rate against S0t-speed-base (c2-packed-tp4-speed, same image, same window), which costs the arm's extra work per replay (in-trace) or nothing per
# replay (prewarm). The coding tests: single-user coding, concurrent4_code, concurrent4_code_equal, concurrent8_code.
# Duration (estimate): 25 min. Not a stop job.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-6
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4_code,concurrent4_code_equal,concurrent8_code
